💡 **SUGGESTION: Autonyms hardcode the supported-locale list a third time (still open, 4th pass)**

Re-review of HEAD `0ba2e3a`: not addressed by any rework round; duplicates the still-open suggestion threads (rounds 1–3).

The supported locales now live in three places: `appSupportedLocales` (blocks), `AppLocalizations.supportedLocales` (generated), and this switch. If a locale is ever added (say `de`) without touching this switch, Settings will show "System default" as the current language while the app renders in the new language — a silent wrong-state display.

Consider one const map colocated with the cubit so adding a locale is a single-place change:

```dart
// packages/blocks/lib/src/settings/locale_cubit.dart
/// Autonyms of [appSupportedLocales]; shown unchanged in every language.
const appLanguageNames = <Locale, String>{
  Locale('en'): 'English',
  Locale('ru'): 'Русский',
  Locale('es'): 'Español',
};

// lib/pages/settings_page.dart
final languageName = appLanguageNames[locale] ?? l10n.systemLanguage;
```

Optional extra consistency: `MaterialApp.supportedLocales` could reuse the generated `AppLocalizations.supportedLocales` instead of the blocks copy — today the two lists agree on membership but differ in order (generated: en, es, ru; blocks: en, ru, es), a subtle trap for future readers.

